    "source_label": "Example 5.6",
    "question": {
      "text": "Solve the differential equation dy/dx = y/(x − 6).",
      "tex": "\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{y}{x - 6}"
    },
    "steps": [
      {
        "text": "Separate the variables.",
        "tex": "\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{y}{x - 6} \\iff \\frac{dy}{y} = \\frac{dx}{x - 6}"
      },
      {
        "text": "Integrate both sides.",
        "tex": "\\ln|y| = \\ln|x - 6| + c"
      },
      {
        "text": "Write the constant as ln k, with ln k = c, and combine the logarithms.",
        "tex": "\\ln|y| = \\ln|x - 6| + \\ln k = \\ln|k(x - 6)|"
      },
      {
        "text": "Remove the logarithms.",
        "tex": "y = k(x - 6), \\quad k \\text{ a constant (general solution)}"
      }
    ],
    "answer_tex": "y = k(x - 6)",
    "review": {
